        {
          "obligationId": "scenario%3Aread-item::entry%3Aread-item",
          "conclusion": "source_refuted",
          "explanation": "At the declared handler-entry boundary, under the stated premise that current_user is an authenticated active superuser and the existing item's owner differs, read_item loads the item and then applies the denial condition only when current_user.is_superuser is false and the owner IDs differ. For the stated superuser, that condition is false, so execution reaches return item and the cross-owner read is permitted. This conforms to the accepted policy, which allows an authenticated active superuser to read regardless of owner. The conclusion assumes the stated current_user premise; the supplied crop shows the handler's current_user parameter and active-user checks in the dependency crop, but does not by itself prove the upstream CurrentUser binding or its complete authentication wiring. That upstream question is outside the declared-entry boundary and is not needed to decide the handler under the supplied premise.",
          "facts": {
            "entry": [
              {
                "statement": "GET /{id} is handled by read_item, whose handler entry receives current_user and id.",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "path": "backend/app/api/routes/items.py",
                    "startLine": 48,
                    "endLine": 49,
                    "quote": "@router.get(\"/{id}\", response_model=ItemPublic)\ndef read_item(session: SessionDep, current_user: CurrentUser, id: uuid.UUID) -> Any:"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "binding": [
